WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.295
Once upon a time, there was an old woman who longed to make an apple pie.

2
00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:12.515
She had plenty of flour, butter, sugar, and cinnamon, but she didn't have any apples.

3
00:00:12.516 --> 00:00:16.015
All she had was a tree full of plums.

4
00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:21.145
The more the woman thought about that apple pie, the more she craved it.

5
00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:25.784
So one day she filled a basket with her plums and headed down the road.

6
00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:31.829
"I will find someone who will trade me some apples for my plums!" she said.

7
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.981
The old woman had walked only a short distance when she spotted a young woman in a yard.

8
00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:39.970
Perhaps this young woman would barter with her.

9
00:00:39.971 --> 00:00:42.684
The old woman called to the young woman.

10
00:00:42.685 --> 00:00:49.731
"Excuse me. Do you have any apples? My heart is set on making an apple pie.

11
00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:55.791
I will give you my whole basket of plums in exchange for some apples."

12
00:00:55.792 --> 00:01:01.562
The young woman shook her head. "I don't have any apples," she said regretfully.

13
00:01:01.563 --> 00:01:06.340
"However, my husband adores plum jelly with his cooked goose.

14
00:01:06.341 --> 00:01:10.569
"Will you take a bag of feathers in exchange for your plums?"

15
00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:16.441
"One pleased is better than two disappointed," the old woman declared.

16
00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:20.230
Soon the old woman had exchanged her plums for the feathers.

17
00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:26.744
Then she walked down a hill and came upon a garden bursting with beautiful lilies, lilacs, and roses.

18
00:01:26.745 --> 00:01:30.828
The old woman paused at the gate to admire the flowers.

19
00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:34.854
Nearby she heard a man and a woman arguing loudly.

20
00:01:34.855 --> 00:01:37.316
"Cotton!" said the woman.

21
00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:40.003
"Straw!" insisted the man.

22
00:01:40.004 --> 00:01:44.532
The couple continued arguing until the woman finally spotted the visitor.

23
00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:47.465
"Look," the woman said to her husband.

24
00:01:47.466 --> 00:01:52.518
"There is an old woman at our gate. Perhaps she can settle our dispute."

25
00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:56.017
"It's worth a try," he agreed.

26
00:01:56.018 --> 00:01:59.666
"Excuse me," the wife called to the old woman.

27
00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:07.530
"If you were making a pillow for your grandfather's bed, would you stuff it with cotton or straw?"

28
00:02:07.531 --> 00:02:11.304
"Neither," the old woman responded briskly.

29
00:02:11.305 --> 00:02:17.854
"I would stuff it with feathers. A feather pillow is fit for a king," she continued.

30
00:02:17.855 --> 00:02:24.116
"In fact, I have a bag of feathers that I would happily trade for some apples."

31
00:02:24.117 --> 00:02:31.233
The husband and wife exchanged glances. They had no apples, but perhaps they could offer the old woman something else.

32
00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:37.355
Soon, with a bouquet of lovely flowers in her basket, the old woman was on her way again.

33
00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:41.090
After traveling for a while, she encountered a handsome lord.

34
00:02:41.091 --> 00:02:43.644
The young man seemed full of despair.

35
00:02:43.645 --> 00:02:49.929
"My lord," inquired the old woman, "why do you look so sad?"

36
00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.661
"I promised to meet my lady," he replied solemnly.

37
00:02:53.662 --> 00:02:56.821
"But I have forgotten the ring I intended to give her.

38
00:02:56.822 --> 00:03:00.577
Now I must go to my love empty-handed."

39
00:03:00.578 --> 00:03:05.419
"You shall have a gift for your lady," the old woman declared.

40
00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:14.598
"I was hoping to barter these flowers for some apples, but love is certainly more delicious than an apple pie."

41
00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:18.166
With a flourish, she presented the bouquet to the young lord.

42
00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.800
The lord's face instantly brightened.

43
00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:24.551
"Thank you!" he said to the old woman, overcome with gratitude.

44
00:03:24.552 --> 00:03:32.517
"However, I cannot accept such a beautiful gift without giving you something in return. Here, please take my gold chain."

45
00:03:32.518 --> 00:03:35.002
It was the woman's turn to be delighted.

46
00:03:35.003 --> 00:03:45.513
"With this precious gold chain, I can buy all the apples in the king's market, and still have some money left over!" she thought.

47
00:03:45.514 --> 00:03:48.957
She hurried to town as fast as her feet could carry her.

48
00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:54.190
She had almost arrived at the market when she noticed a poor mother huddled with her children.

49
00:03:54.191 --> 00:03:57.873
"My children are starving," the mother murmured.

50
00:03:57.874 --> 00:04:02.223
"We have no food, and I have no money."

51
00:04:02.224 --> 00:04:06.156
The old woman glimpsed the precious gold chain in her basket.

52
00:04:06.157 --> 00:04:14.231
"Never shall someone say that I made apple pie for dinner and let my neighbor starve," she said softly.

53
00:04:14.232 --> 00:04:20.197
Slowly, she reached into the basket for the chain.

54
00:04:20.198 --> 00:04:23.493
The old woman headed for home with her empty basket.

55
00:04:23.494 --> 00:04:28.978
She had not walked very far when the poor mother and her children chased after her.

56
00:04:28.979 --> 00:04:32.694
"We have only one thing to give you," said the mother.

57
00:04:32.695 --> 00:04:38.511
"Please take this puppy. His love will be a reminder of our appreciation."

58
00:04:38.512 --> 00:04:44.815
The old woman thanked the family, and then gently placed the puppy in the basket.

59
00:04:44.816 --> 00:04:50.656
As she turned a corner, she saw a tall tree—laden with ripe, juicy apples!

60
00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:54.753
Nearby stood an old man.

61
00:04:54.754 --> 00:04:59.757
"That's a fine tree of apples," the old woman called to him.

62
00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:06.184
The man nodded and looked away. "Yes, it's a fine tree, but I have no one to share it with.

63
00:05:06.185 --> 00:05:11.223
My wife died years ago, and all of my children live far away."

64
00:05:11.224 --> 00:05:15.366
Just then the puppy barked and poked his head out of the basket.

65
00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:18.804
The lonely old man beamed at the sight of the puppy.

66
00:05:18.805 --> 00:05:23.774
The old woman smiled too. A wonderful idea had occurred to her.

67
00:05:23.775 --> 00:05:27.348
Soon the old woman was walking toward home again.

68
00:05:27.349 --> 00:05:31.549
At last her basket was filled with apples for a pie.

69
00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:46.648
"If you try long enough and hard enough," she said contentedly, "you will get some apples for plums."

